        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: l'impact",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "l'impact — \"the impact\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ce projet a un impact sur tout le quartier. This project has an impact on the whole neighbourhood."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Avoir un impact sur — to have an effect on. The final ct is said. Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "impact comes from Latin impāctus, the participle of impingere \"to dash against, to strike\" (Lewis & Short), built on pangere \"to fix, to drive in\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
